    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_act_dont_just_scroll_title">Act, Don’t Just Scroll!</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_act_dont_just_scroll_description_1">➤ Doom-scrolling — spending hours passively consuming negative content — lowers your mood, increases stress and anxiety, and weakens self-esteem (Mental Health Warning, The Sun).</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_act_dont_just_scroll_description_2">➤ A Canadian study shows that more than 2 hours a day of passive scrolling doubles teens’ risk of anxiety (Passive Scrolling Study, EurekAlert).</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_act_dont_just_scroll_description_3">➤ The New Yorker also highlights how this “doom-loop” feeds a negative spiral and makes us more passive in real life (Doomscrolling Is Slowly Eroding Your Soul, New Yorker).</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_act_dont_just_scroll_button">Continue</string>

    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_sedentary_life_title">Sedentary Life Hurts Your Health</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_sedentary_life_description_1">➤ Spending more than 12 hours a day sitting raises your risk of early death by 38%, unless you add at least 22 minutes of moderate activity daily (Le Monde).</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_sedentary_life_description_2">➤ Staying still also affects your heart: a study on 11–24-year-olds showed more heart mass, less heart function (Le Monde).</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_sedentary_life_description_3">➤ Being inactive cuts your social interactions, feeds instant gratification (screens), and weakens your mind (anxiety, mood, focus).</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_sedentary_life_button">Continue</string>

    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_explore_world_title">Explore the World, Transform Your Life</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_explore_world_description_1">➤ The best cure for a sedentary life? Go out, discover, explore.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_explore_world_description_2">➤ Mentally, just a few minutes in nature can lower stress, boost your mood, creativity, and focus (Time, PubMed).</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_explore_world_description_3">➤ Socially, walking with others or joining outdoor activities strengthens your sense of belonging, builds connection, and reduces loneliness (Grow Therapy).</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_explore_world_description_4">➤ Physically, even short city walks (15–20 min a day) boost your heart health, balance your energy, and reduce long-term health risks (PopSugar).</string>
    <string name="onboarding_educational_content_explore_world_button">Continue</string>

