    <string name="quote_title">Did you know?</string>
    <string name="cita_one_quebec_chateaufrontenac_1">🏰 Château Frontenac. Built in 1893 by the Canadian Pacific Railway company to attract wealthy travelers.</string>
    <string name="cita_one_quebec_chateaufrontenac_2">🏰 Château Frontenac.It is the most photographed hotel in the world 📸.</string>
    <string name="cita_one_quebec_chateaufrontenac_3">🏰 Château Frontenac. The movie “Catch Me If You Can” (2002, starring Leonardo DiCaprio &amp; Tom Hanks) filmed some scenes inside.</string>

    <string name="cita_one_montreal_vieuxmontreal_1">🎬 Old Montreal &amp; Downtown. Old Montreal has been used as a backdrop for several Hollywood films, including The Curious Case of Benjamin Button (2008).</string>

    <string name="cita_one_quebec_pontquebec_1">🌉 Quebec Bridge. Built in 1917, it is the longest cantilever bridge in the world.</string>
    <string name="cita_one_quebec_pontquebec_2">🌉 Quebec Bridge. Unfortunately, its history is marked by two collapses (1907 &amp; 1916), which killed more than 80 workers.</string>

    <string name="cita_one_montreal_placedesarts_1">🎭 Place des Arts. The largest cultural and artistic complex in Canada.</string>
    <string name="cita_one_montreal_placedesarts_2">🎭 Place des Arts. This is where Leonard Cohen gave some of his legendary concerts.</string>

    <string name="cita_one_saguenay_fjord_1">🌲 Saguenay Fjord. It is one of the only inhabited fjords in North America.</string>
    <string name="cita_one_saguenay_fjord_2">🌲 Saguenay Fjord. The cliffs sometimes reach 400 meters high.</string>
    <string name="cita_one_saguenay_fjord_3">🌲 Saguenay Fjord. Humpback whales and belugas often come here to feed 🐋.</string>

    <string name="cita_one_montreal_oratoire_1">⛪ Saint Joseph’s Oratory. Founded in 1904 by Brother André, canonized in 2010.</string>
    <string name="cita_one_montreal_oratoire_2">⛪ Saint Joseph’s Oratory. It is the largest shrine in the world dedicated to Saint Joseph.</string>
    <string name="cita_one_montreal_oratoire_3">⛪ Saint Joseph’s Oratory. Its dome is the 2nd largest in the world after St. Peter’s Basilica in Rome.</string>

    <string name="cita_one_monteregie_montst_hilaire_1">🍁 Mont Saint-Hilaire. First UNESCO biosphere reserve in Canada (1978).</string>
    <string name="cita_one_monteregie_montst_hilaire_2">🍁 Mont Saint-Hilaire. Very popular for its apples 🍎 → apple picking has been organized here for generations.</string>

    <string name="cita_one_montreal_stadeolympique_1">🏟️ Olympic Stadium. Built for the 1976 Games, it cost over $1 billion and took 30 years to pay off.</string>
    <string name="cita_one_montreal_stadeolympique_2">🏟️ Olympic Stadium. The dive by Greg Louganis in 1984 remains one of the most iconic moments.</string>

